  "userDescription": "To resolve a user's topic or metric reference, call semantic_search('<core concept phrase>') FIRST. Use the returned ref (metric_id or term_id) for any further lookups in other sources. Report total_matches when more matched than shown. closeness is relative similarity — never present it as a probability. If semantic_search returns no rows, say the certified knowledge base has nothing sufficiently related; do not guess.\n\nFor LINEAGE questions - which metrics use/read a table, or filter on/select a column - call readers_of_table('<table>') or column_usage('<column>'). These read parsed SQL lineage edges; NEVER answer lineage by name similarity or hand-written LIKE queries (the catalog contains deliberate name-cousins). The matched column discloses exact vs token matching; the distinct ref count is the exact answer to 'how many metrics'.\n",
